The "run" is the five-step decision tree + three scenario analyses, authored
and self-reviewed in-session against NIST SP 800-86 (forensic techniques in
IR; csrc landing fetched 2026-10-10, 45,371 bytes) and the DOJ CCIPS remit
pages (justice.gov, fetched 2026-10-10, 108,033 bytes).

Scope: fictional Copperline Freight. Tree: (1) crime suspected? -> preserve to
criminal standards, counsel, no premature interview; (2) litigation anticipated?
-> litigation hold now, in writing, broad; (3) regulator notification? -> clock
runs on awareness; (4) administrative track in parallel after counsel clears;
(5) reassess at every new fact. Scenarios: A (suspected insider sysadmin) ->
admin + criminal; sequence counsel-first, image-before-touch, no interview yet;
B (ransomware w/ EU customer data exfil) -> regulatory (72h dominates) + civil
+ criminal + admin; hold day one; C (expense fraud) -> admin only, still
preserved properly. Each: type(s), authority, evidence standard, sequencing,
the one mistake to avoid.

